course: dictionary
lesson: 16158
title: Holding something back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To withhold something means to keep it back and not give it. When you withhold information, you know something but you do not tell it. Withhold is a verb, so its forms are withhold, withholds, withheld and withholding.
explain: You can also withhold a payment or a reward. «The shop withheld his pay until the work was finished.» The shop kept his money back until the job was done. The clue is the word until: the money came later, not straight away.
explain: Money can be withheld before you get it too. Tax is taken from a worker's wages, so they never receive that part. «Tax is withheld from Dad's wages before he gets paid.» Look for clue words like keep back, refuse and hold back.
fact: Withhold means to keep something back and refuse to give it.
fact: «Withhold information» means you know something and do not share it.
fact: «Withhold payment» means keeping money back until something happens, such as a job being finished.
fact: «Withheld number» means a phone call where the caller has hidden their number.
fact: Tax is withheld from wages, so workers get their pay after part of it has been kept back.
exercise: «The shop withheld his pay until the work was finished.» What does withheld mean here? | Spent it on a gift | Sent it by post | Gave it all early | *Kept it back until later
exercise: «Please do not withhold the truth from me.» What does withhold mean? | Tell it loudly | *Keep it back and do not give it | Forget it quickly | Write it on a card
exercise: Your phone shows «withheld number» for a call. What does that mean? | The call is free | The phone is broken | *The caller has hidden their number | The number is written on a sticker
test: «Tax is withheld from Dad's wages before he gets paid.» What is kept back from his pay? | Extra holidays | His lunch money | A bonus | *Part of his pay, for tax
test: «If someone asks you to withhold something that makes you feel unsafe, what should you do?» | *Tell a trusted adult | Keep it secret forever | Wait and see | Hide it under the bed
exam: What does withhold mean? | To give something freely | To shout at someone | *To keep something back and not give it | To tell everyone loudly
